@article{ WOS:001318538200015,
Author = {Mocanu, George Danut and Murariu, Gabriel},
Title = {The Importance of Basketball for High School Students. Part 2 (Utility
   Dimension Analysis)},
Journal = {REVISTA ROMANEASCA PENTRU EDUCATIE MULTIDIMENSIONALA},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {16},
Number = {2},
Pages = {271-299},
Month = {JUN},
Abstract = {Background and Study Purpose. The use of basketball in curricular and
   extracurricular activities is common in most countries. The research
   aims to identify the opinions of high school students and the effects
   and usefulness of basketball on multiple levels: socialization, stress
   reduction, health and fitness optimization, personality formation, body
   harmony, etc. Material and Methods. A sample of 259 high school students
   (124 females and 135 males) from Gorj county, Romania, were included in
   a sociometric cross-sectional study in the first part of the 2023-2024
   school year. All investigated participants partook in physical education
   lessons with basketball topics. The factor analysis of the applied
   questionnaire included 14 items within the usefulness dimension, with
   responses reported on a Likert scale with 5 levels of intensity of
   opinions. The independent Gender, Area variables and the interaction
   Gender {*}Area variables were defined and analysed. Results. Gender
   differences indicate higher values for males, but not statistically
   significant (P > 0.05). Only for flexibility is the opinion of females
   superior and statistically significant (P < 0.05). Differences between
   urban and rural are in favour or urban for most items, but still
   statistically insignificant (P > 0.05). The only items where F values
   are significant are those related to the role of basketball in the
   formation of fair-play attitude and the accessibility of basketball as a
   leisure activity (P < 0.05). The Gender {*}Area variables interaction
   indicates only 3 situations where significant differences of opinion are
   reported (P < 0.05): accessibility of basketball as a leisure activity,
   effect on effort capacity and fitness level, and effect of basketball on
   coordination. All these cases indicate higher values of urban males vs
   rural males and vice versa for females, where rural females score higher
   than urban females. Conclusions. For the utility dimension, we noted the
   majority of opinions in favour of basketball, through its various
   effects on students in adolescence. The most optimistic scores were for
   the benefits of coordination and speed (components of skill-related
   physical fitness). This is followed by beneficial effects on health, the
   formation of fair-play attitudes, physical development and body harmony,
   facilitating socialization, communication and group integration. The
   influence of basketball on stress reduction is also viewed with
   confidence. The effect on improving effort capacity and general level of
   physical fitness scores moderately. Weaker values are given for
   influences on intellectual abilities and level of segmental muscle
   strength. Students give the lowest confidence in the effects of
   basketball on flexibility and endurance levels. In contrast to the
   attractiveness factor, for the usefulness dimension, we found less
   significant differences in opinion between rural and urban females and
   males. This is an indicator of critical thinking ability and reflects a
   good level of understanding of the effects of playing basketball on
   multiple levels in the sample surveyed.},
