Pages = {383-408},
Abstract = {Children at Risk: The Role of Commissions for the Protection of Minors
   in Portugal
   Since children have been acknowledged as an autonomous social group, it
   has become necessary to create adequate laws to protect their
   fundamental rights, including the right to education, health, and
   affection. However, despite significant progress for childhood
   worldwide, children's fundamental rights are still not ensured. It is
   thus important to reflect on the way laws for the protection of children
   have developed, analyzing their original objectives and principles and
   the means used in their enforcement. This article discusses the role of
   the Commissions for the Protection of Minors at Social Risk in Portugal.},
